            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical aspects of appendicitis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>243-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>When evaluating 4232 appendectomies between 1977-1986 there were 12.5% perforations and in 19.3% the diagnosis was not justified. In 5.1% surgical intervention was done without acute appendicitis. The overall lethality was 0.5%, the cases of perforation 2.3%. The diagnosis of lethality was cardiopulmonary disease. In this follow up study we discuss possibilities of giving a secure diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
